  "prefLabel": "Phy 302.04 Direct personal supervision",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 302.04 “Direct personal supervision” means, pursuant to RSA 328-A:2, III, namely, “that the physical therapist or the physical therapist assistant is physically present and immediately available to direct and supervise tasks that are related to patient/client management. The direction and supervision is continuous throughout the time these tasks are performed. Telecommunications does not meet the requirement of direct personal supervision.”\n\nSource. #9233, eff 8-22-08; ss by #10933, eff 9-18-15; ss by #12864, eff 9-10-19; ss by #14563, eff 6-20-26, EXPIRES: 6-20-36",
